                <pb facs="0395" n="1463" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1463"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>
                    Mendès-France and Adenauer engaged in discussions on the
                    Saar following dinner on October 22, discussions that lasted until <pb
                        facs="0396" n="1464" xml:id="pg1464"/> 3 a.m. the following morning.
                    Telegram 1711 from Paris, October 23, briefly noted that “agreement had been
                    practically reached on political points with only one or two economic problems
                    (coal mines and steel works) outstanding” (762.022/10–2354). They met again at
                    11:30 a.m. on October 23 and completed their negotiations on the Saar by
                    reaching an agreement. No records of the meetings on October 22 and 23 were
                    found in the Department of State files which would provide information
                    concerning the details of these negotiations. For the text of the Agreement
                    between the Government of the Federal Republic of Germany and the Government of
                    the French Republic on the Saar Statute, Paris, October 23, 1954, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Documents</hi> (R.I.I.A.) for 1954, pages 116–118. For
                    the accompanying exchange of letters, see <hi rendition="#italic">Notes et
                        Etudes Documentaires No. 1951</hi>, 23 Novembre 1954.</p>
            </div>
